  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. Its first run succeeded.\n\n**1. What's in the data** (`kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`)\n- 14,074 web requests, timestamped from 2026\u201110\u201104 to 2026\u201112\u201103. The sample data includes future dates.\n- Status codes: 12,832 are `200`, 801 are `404` and 441 are `503`. That's an 8.8% error rate, and 503 is the only 5xx code present.\n- The requests go to 4 hosts (mostly `artifacts.elastic.co` and `www.elastic.co`) and come from 1,001 client IPs.\n- Each record includes response size in `bytes` (about 5.7 KB on average), destination country (`geo.dest`, led by CN, IN and US), file type (`extension`), OS and user agent.\n- The status code is stored as text, so the queries use its `response.keyword` subfield.\n\n**2. Dashboard \"EFF-7e77521d Web logs overview\"** (id `62b2c0b2-c14b-41e9-9158-1e30493df235`)\nIt has 9 panels. I ran each panel's query directly and all of them return data.\n- **Top row of headline numbers:** total requests, unique visitors, error rate (%), and average bytes per request.\n- **Requests over time by response code:** a stacked bar chart.\n- **Bytes transferred over time:** a line chart.\n- **Top lists:** top 10 destination countries, requests per host, and top file extensions.\n\nThe default time range is the last 7 days. The headline numbers and top lists cover the whole dataset and don't change with the dashboard's time picker. Only the two time charts follow the selected range.\n\n**3. Rule \"EFF-7e77521d 5xx spike\"** (id `d94f51d3-b3b0-43d7-8afa-d69661093df2`)\n- It's an Elasticsearch query rule on the \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" data view.\n- It matches requests where `response.keyword : 5*`, meaning any 5xx code.\n- It checks every minute and fires when more than 10 such requests arrive within 5 minutes.\n\nThe rule has no notification actions, so an alert will show in Kibana's Alerts view but won't send an email or message anywhere. If you want notifications, I can add a connector to the rule.",
